      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear how unhelpful that advice feels when you are facing this profound sense of hollowness.\nWhen the \"math\" of your life suddenly no longer adds up, no advice about \"hope\" can fix that feeling because the foundation is gone.\nYou are not alone in feeling this deep emptiness, and the fact that \"finding hope\" feels like a lie only means you are honest about the pain.\nPlease consider that you can be comforted by the reality that you, too, are a part of life, even if the meaning you thought it should be is no longer there.\nYou can reach out to a counseling service just to be heard without the pressure of \"fixing\" anything, where you can feel safe in this void.",
